; GLQuakePlayNull -- GLQuake's play benchmark (-playbench: e1m1 played by a
; script with a fixed frame time, the server included) on the null card,
; three times with one binary: the play caches off (-noplaycache), on, and
; on again. Equal "playbench state" checksums = the caches change nothing
; and the game is repeatable. Needs: gmake glquake glquake-data rgl-lib
; (glquake-data copies GLQuake's playbench.txt, the e1m1 play script, to
; dist/Quake/id1).
; LIMIT 1800
FailAt 1000
Wait 12
Stack 1000000
Delete >NIL: DEV:Test/play-#?
Echo "=== off ===" >DEV:Test/auto.log
Run >NIL: Execute DEV:Test/RunPlayB GLQuake off 600 -anycpu -noplaycache
Execute DEV:Test/WaitDone DEV:Test/play-off.done
Search DEV:Test/play-off.log "playbench" NONUM >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Search DEV:Test/play-off.log "rc=" NONUM >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Echo "=== on ===" >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Run >NIL: Execute DEV:Test/RunPlayB GLQuake on 600 -anycpu
Execute DEV:Test/WaitDone DEV:Test/play-on.done
Search DEV:Test/play-on.log "playbench" NONUM >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Search DEV:Test/play-on.log "rc=" NONUM >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Echo "=== on again ===" >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Run >NIL: Execute DEV:Test/RunPlayB GLQuake on2 600 -anycpu
Execute DEV:Test/WaitDone DEV:Test/play-on2.done
Search DEV:Test/play-on2.log "playbench" NONUM >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Search DEV:Test/play-on2.log "rc=" NONUM >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Echo "=== done ===" >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Echo >DEV:Test/AutoDone done
